; shelf-science.kb -- Sky and Science, a shelf: read in only when the sky, the stars, the quantum, or the climate is first
; asked about. Begun from the questions patty-cake's pupils asked and Nuage could not answer (3 xi 2026).
(comment AstronomicalObject "a natural thing out in space, such as a star, a planet, a moon, or a galaxy") (word AstronomicalObject "astronomical object" "astronomical objects" "heavenly body" "heavenly bodies")
(genls Star AstronomicalObject) (genls Planet AstronomicalObject) (genls Moon AstronomicalObject)
(genls BlackHole AstronomicalObject) (word BlackHole "black hole" "black holes")
(comment BlackHole "a place in space where gravity pulls so hard that nothing, not even light, can get out. Most form when a very large star collapses at the end of its life")
(why BlackHole "its gravity is so strong that not even light can escape it, so it gives off no light of its own")
(prop BlackHole origin "from very large stars that collapse at the end of their lives")
(genls Nebula Cloud) (word Nebula "nebula" "nebulae" "nebulas")
(comment Nebula "a vast cloud of gas and dust in space, where stars are born")
(prop Star origin "from nebulae, clouds of gas and dust that collapse under their own gravity until their centres grow hot enough to fuse hydrogen")
(why Star "gravity squeezes a cloud of gas until its centre grows hot enough to fuse hydrogen into helium, and the energy of that fusion makes it shine")
(why Star "their light crosses moving layers of air on its way down, and each layer bends it a little differently, so it seems to flicker. Planets, which show a tiny disc, twinkle less")
(genls Galaxy AstronomicalObject) (word Galaxy "galaxy" "galaxies")
(comment Galaxy "a vast gathering of stars, gas, and dust, held together by gravity. Ours is the Milky Way")
(unique Universe) (word Universe "universe" "cosmos")
(comment Universe "everything that exists: all of space and time, and all the matter and energy in them. It is still expanding")
(prop Universe origin "from the Big Bang, about 13.8 billion years ago, and it is still expanding")
(unique BigBang) (word BigBang "big bang" "big bang theory")
(comment BigBang "the beginning of the universe as far back as it can be traced, about 13.8 billion years ago, when everything was extremely hot and dense and began to expand. It was not an explosion in space, but the stretching of space itself")
(genls Quantum Energy) (word Quantum "quantum" "quanta")
(comment Quantum "the smallest amount of something, such as energy or light, that can exist on its own. Light comes in quanta called photons")
(mass QuantumPhysics) (word QuantumPhysics "quantum physics" "quantum mechanics" "quantum theory")
(comment QuantumPhysics "the science of how very small things, such as atoms and light, behave. At that size, things come in quanta, and can be in a blend of states until they are measured")
(word Qubit "qubit" "qubits")
(comment Qubit "the unit of a quantum computer. An ordinary bit is 0 or 1, but a qubit can be in a blend of both until it is measured")
(genls QuantumComputer Computer) (word QuantumComputer "quantum computer" "quantum computers")
(comment QuantumComputer "a computer built of qubits, which can work some problems in ways an ordinary computer cannot")
(word Climate "climate" "climates") (comment Climate "the usual weather of a place, taken over many years")
(mass ClimateChange) (word ClimateChange "climate change" "global warming")
(comment ClimateChange "the long, slow change of the Earth's climate. Today the Earth is warming, mostly because burning coal, oil, and gas adds heat-trapping gases to the air")
(why ClimateChange "gases such as carbon dioxide trap heat in the air, which is the greenhouse effect, and burning coal, oil, and gas adds more of them")
(unique GreenhouseEffect) (word GreenhouseEffect "greenhouse effect")
(comment GreenhouseEffect "the warming of a planet by gases in its air, such as water vapour and carbon dioxide, which let sunlight in but keep some heat from getting out. Without it, the Earth would be frozen")
